MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_001: Hey, Creek. Any chance I can hear another one of\nyour stories?
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_002: Of course. Shall I regale you with another of my\npast battles?
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_003: Sure. I was just reading Arago: Chronicles of the\nWestern War, and you're in it.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_004: I'd love to get your firsthand account of how you\ntook the impenetrable mountain fortress.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_005: Ah, that. Well, first we dispatched scouts to find an\nunguarded route to the castle. Once that was done...
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_006: I see. So that's how you captured it. This gives me a\nlot to think about.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_007: The way you tell the story, I can see every detail.\nIt's like I'm right there.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_008: One of the perks of eyewitness testimony. I'm glad\nyou appreciated the tale.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_009: Official records only retain the grandest of exploits.\nThey often print the legend, not the truth.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_010: I'm pleased that you looked beyond those weighty\ntomes for a firsthand account of the tactics involved.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_011: You're pleased? I'm the one who gets to hear your\nwonderful stories.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_012: But there's so much more I want to ask. Like, when\nyou pursued the retreating army...
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_013: I am so sorry. I've kept you talking for way too long.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_014: I don't mind. Especially since you shared your own\nstories of the Great August.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_015: You're so kind to want to hear about my grandpa.\nMy stories just kept going and going.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_016: But how interesting could it be to hear about our life\nout in the sticks?
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_017: Don't sell yourself short. It was fascinating to hear of\nthe Great August as a man, rather than a prodigy.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_018: Interesting way to put it. Did you know him?
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_019: Heh. You couldn't have known, but all that I learned\nof tactics came from your grandfather.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_020: In his days at Arago, he would give lessons to\nthe squires.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_021: Really? But Creek, your tactics are diametrically\nopposed from what Grandpa taught.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_022: Which is odd, since he laid the foundations of\nArago's modern strategy and you studied under him.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_023: So how did you become a knight of Arago while\nfighting in a completely different style?
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_024: It's because I was eager to outsmart my mentor from\nthe first. He found it quite irritating.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_025: Hahaha. You just have to prove your own ideas, don't\nyou? That makes you even more interesting.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_026: I'll take that as a compliment. But I ask that you not\nmention this to the Great August.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_027: If he knew I was filling his beloved granddaughter's\nhead with skulduggery, I'd never hear the end of it.
MID_SE_Tia_Hri_C_028: I'll keep your secret, Creek, but you'll have to tell me\na lot more about yourself.